  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man in cowboy attire",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man standing in front of the wagon. The phrase 'long time no see' at the top of the image is implicitly directed at the man, creating a deictic projection where the user sees themselves as the one who has 'seen' or is reconnecting with the man. This projection is reinforced by the hateful context of the racial slur 'nigger' at the bottom, which frames the man as the target of the user's hateful intent. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the spatial and textual framing (text above the man, slur below) creates an implicit projection of the user as the one initiating the 'long time no see' greeting and as the one who is projecting the hateful slur onto the man.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
